    "body": "(Feedback welcome, also don't really like the option name 'mcfollow' ...)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nProblem:\r\n- gQ does not restore follow-mode (q=).\r\n- Users/plugins have no way to check if follow-mode is enabled.\r\n\r\nSolution:\r\nIntroduce buffer-local option ~~'mcfollow'~~ 'follow'.\r\n\r\nfix https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41647",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-27T14:03:52Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Aside from the name sounding like a rapper, I like it. As I understand it, there's only one option that shares the `mc` prefix: `maxcombine` (`mco`).\r\n\r\nI just don't know whether this option should be buffer-specific or namespaced under `vim.v`, since it behaves globally.",
            "created_at": "2026-09-25T19:40:58Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/42095#issuecomment-5838489670",
            "id": 5838489670,
            "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/42095",
            "minimized": null,
            "node_id": "IC_kwDOAPphoM8AAAABXABIRg",
