        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> since it behaves globally.\r\n\r\nIt's buffer-local (inherits global default), as are cursors. Multiple buffers can have cursors at any time.\r\n\r\nBeing buffer-local allows `gQ` to \"inherit\" whatever the last `q=` was for that buffer.",
            "created_at": "2026-09-25T20:17:32Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/42095#issuecomment-5838968401",
            "id": 5838968401,
